# Copy to .env.local for `bun run dev`, or pass with `docker run --env-file`.
# Every data source is free and keyless. Only the AI parts need a key.

# OpenRouter (https://openrouter.ai/keys) writes the traveler message and answers the chat,
# from the assessment only. It never sets the risk level. Server-side only.
# Without it, the assessment still works and the page says the AI parts are off.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=google/gemma-4-31b-it:free
# OPENROUTER_FALLBACK_MODELS=google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it:free   (tried when the first is rate-limited)
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1   (any OpenAI-compatible endpoint)

# api.weather.gov asks for a contact in the User-Agent.
# NWS_USER_AGENT=travel-risk (you@example.com)
